# Supervisor chat

- If the supervisor’s wording, spelling, or grammar would change the meaning, **restate the intended meaning in one sentence** and use that meaning. Persist the mapping if it is a standing term.
- **More than one open question:** ask **one** question, wait for the answer, then the next. Do not batch questions.
- Same turn, write every grouping lock into `docs/order-grouping-sorter/order-grouping-locks.md`.

Standing terms (always-on):

- **commit and push** (git) = supervisor asks in chat → agent commits the local delta (respect `.gitignore`; skip debug/temp/run junk) and pushes `main` to **both** remotes: `origin` (`areebxi/Warehouse-Operations-System`) and `daataa` (`DaataaDirect/Warehouse-Operations-System`). Not scheduled; not automatic. Author via one-shot `git -c user.name` / `user.email` (**Areeb Yaqub** / `46938981+areebxi@users.noreply.github.com`) — do not rewrite global git config. Locked 2026-09-29; dual remote 2026-10-26.
- **run the group sorter** / **group my awaiting shipment** / **run the sorter** = straight `--run` on the current ShipStation `awaiting_shipment` pool into the shift the supervisor already named in that message (no catalog seed, no packing dry-run first; short report when done). An order still awaiting is processed even if an earlier shift CSV already has it. If that message does not name the shift, **ask which shift** and do not run yet. This applies in every chat and every new session, not only the conversation that locked it. Locked 2026-10-14; catalog step removed 2026-10-20. Detail: `.cursor/rules/order-grouping-sorter/approval.mdc`.
- **add unmatched** = run `Order Grouping Sorter/scripts/seed_catalog_misses.py` only (Areeb append via `add_labels.py --csv`; no Packing Input write). Locked 2026-10-20.
- **1st–5th shift tag** (ShipStation, exact names): `001-1st Shift`, `002-2nd Shift`, `003-3rd Shift`, `004-4th Shift`, `005-5th Shift`. Locked 2026-10-14. Sorter intake still ignores these tags when choosing the shift folder.
- **put the {1st–5th} shift tag on these files** = run `Order Grouping Sorter/scripts/tag_shift_orders.py --shift {1st|2nd|3rd|4th|5th}` on the CSVs named in that message, immediately. Do not look up the API again. The script skips orders that already have the tag, posts in parallel (8 workers), and pauses when ShipStation’s rate-limit window is nearly empty. Locked 2026-10-18; parallel 2026-10-20.

Grouping vocabulary (batch, shift, fixed batch, today/ship-by, finish gates, B50/B100, …): `.cursor/rules/order-grouping-sorter/standing-terms.mdc` + `docs/order-grouping-sorter/order-grouping-locks.md`. Load with sorter / locks work — not every chat.

Catalog fill terms (Supply Method, Printing Type, Supplier Name, Areeb, BTC/Uneek/Absolute paths): `.cursor/rules/custom-label-database/` (+ `global/cl-sku-match.mdc`). Packing later / missing-logo reprint: `.cursor/rules/order-packing-list-generator/`.
